  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive a 2D integer array `tasks` where `tasks[i] = [si, ti]`.\n\nEach `[si, ti]` in `tasks` represents a task with start time `si` that takes `ti` units of time to finish.\n\nOutput the earliest time at which no fewer than one task is finished.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n**Input:** tasks = [[1,6],[2,3]]\n\n**Output:** 5\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nThe first task starts at time `t = 1` and finishes at time `1 + 6 = 7`. The second task finishes at time `2 + 3 = 5`. You can finish one task at time 5.\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n**Input:** tasks = [[100,100],[100,100],[100,100]]\n\n**Output:** 200\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nAll three tasks finish at time `100 + 100 = 200`.\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= tasks.length <= 100`\n* `tasks[i] = [si, ti]`\n* `1 <= si, ti <= 100`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
